Experimental fixed empty-auth startup retirement; not applied by Context Foundry.
Target: can1357/oh-my-pi @ 24439066040e006eb08da7b204f0ac41c79d2de9
Owner: 003 T006, bounded-pilot-v2 startup observation and admission.
Requires prior caller/auth/refusal/restricted/catalog/settings patches.
Modules: AuthStorage::retireStartupEmptyAuth; auth/startup-empty::EmptyStartupAuth;
SqliteAuthCredentialStore scalar empty/closed checks; CredentialPool::reload;
auth-broker/discover::resolveAuthBrokerConfig; CLI explicit flag and SDK original binding.
Tests: startup-empty-auth.test.ts, original auth suites, main/CLI/restricted SDK suites.
Difference: explicit --startup-empty-auth requires --restrict-tools. The actual local
SQLite store and original supported calls remain; no facade or credential values are
returned. Source guards reject material/broker/foreign backend and unsupported methods.
The finite namespace owner joins original returned promises and completion observers,
including cached references and fresh lookups after a supported instrumentation change.
Metadata identity and local no-op usage completion consumers remain available after close.
Unknown calls or policy violations cannot obtain a retirement receipt. At most 4096 starts.
Ordinary auth remains outside the opt-in profile. The exact original auth instance is bound
to the sealed SDK session/registry after original auth/settings-link retirement.
No general OAuth drain, physical FD release, complete inventory, Ready, transport permission,
paid execution or release signing is established. Native/source receipts are dated in validation.

